{
  "schemaVersion": "northstar.web:unbound-permission-acknowledgement/v1",
  "header": [
    "THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. Every permission below is declared by the release input beside this file and bound to NO evaluator: every production CurrentPolicyGateway returns ALLOW (program review 2026-08-20, finding R7). Listing a permission here acknowledges that vacuum by name so the release still builds; it does not authorize anything.",
    "An entry leaves when queue row 7 (the policy/identity kernel) binds its permission to an evaluator, or when the permission itself leaves the package. Row 7 empties this list, and when the last entry is gone the refusal is absolute: no declared permission compiles without an evaluator binding. Shrinking is a review policy over this file; the compiler enforces the snapshot invariant that every entry is true of the package it is handed with.",
    "The release scripts beside this file read it and hand each package its own entries through CompilerExecutionOptions.unboundPermissionAcknowledgement. A permission that is declared and NOT listed refuses the release build by name (COMPILER_PERMISSION_EVALUATOR_UNBOUND). An entry that names a permission the package no longer declares on that resource, one an evaluator now binds, or a duplicate, refuses it too (COMPILER_PERMISSION_ACKNOWLEDGEMENT_STALE). A package with no key here cannot be built by those scripts at all: the loader refuses before compiling. Adding an entry is a deliberate act a reviewer reads; it is never generated."
  ],
